From af2f7058005c06f5ff32711f72b78d5e09f49b3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:48:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/38] WIP HC16: skip the dead F32 store when every consumer
 reads the BF16 copy

The graph optimizer now classifies each MMB dense GEMM activation's consumers:
when every one reads it through the MMB bf16 activation cache (a quantized/bf16
MUL_MAT / MUL_MAT_ID, through views), the activation is marked BF16-only and the
producer writes only the BF16 slot copy; otherwise it keeps the F32 output and
adds the BF16 copy as before.  The producers (fused rms_norm+mul, fused
sigmoid/silu+mul, fused scale+unary, generic unary, dsv4_hc_pre) gained a
store_f32 flag so the dead F32 store is skipped.

Bit-identical: PPL c2048 stays 10.6428, greedy 9930c674a6ca unchanged, the
W=1..8 width probe is pure, FLASH_ATTN_QSA / GATED_DELTA_NET pass.

gfx1151 IQ4_XS Flash-Next bf16 KV, -b/-ub 2048, MMB+QSA3: the unary_gated
producer drops 302 -> 229 ms; end to end pp8192 952.4 -> 974.0 (+2.3 %),
pp2048 975.3 -> 1007.4 (+3.3 %) for HC16=1 vs 0 (was +1.3 %/+2.0 % with the
always-emit form).  xn stays on the copy path (dsv4_hc_pre / tiny-M still read
F32), so rms_norm is unchanged.
